{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when…</b> Here he comes to give a reason for his first statement, which was ״אֵין יִרְאַת אֱלֹהִים״ (there is no fear of Elohim). For Avimelekh might say to him: What did you see in this place that you suspected them of having no fear of Elohim? Therefore he said that this precaution he established — to say ״אֲחוֹתִי״ (my sister) — was not for the sake of that place alone, but as a general rule he established this precaution for any place suspected of lacking fear of Elohim. And this doubt never departed from him even regarding Gerar, for even though it has no presumption of ״אֵין יִרְאַת אֱלֹהִים,״ he concedes that Avraham likewise has no presumption in its favor that it does possess fear of Elohim. And from this point Avimelekh's arguments are foreclosed."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:33.535601551Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}